1
00:00:00,174 --> 00:00:03,164
One island makes most of the
world's most advanced chips.

2
00:00:03,314 --> 00:00:04,464
What if it was cut off?

3
00:00:04,570 --> 00:00:08,920
The Taiwan Strait is about 130
kilometres wide at its narrowest,

4
00:00:09,030 --> 00:00:11,540
and it is one of the
busiest sea lanes on Earth.

5
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:15,190
Taiwan makes roughly 90 percent of
the world's most advanced chips,

6
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:18,430
most of them at one company, TSMC.

7
00:00:18,511 --> 00:00:22,781
Phones, cars, servers and artificial
intelligence all depend on them.

8
00:00:23,111 --> 00:00:25,821
A blockade or a conflict could
stop shipments from the island.

9
00:00:25,957 --> 00:00:30,106
Analysts put the cost of a Taiwan
crisis in the trillions of dollars.

10
00:00:30,117 --> 00:00:32,227
India is building its first chip plants,

11
00:00:32,457 --> 00:00:36,647
but they start with older chips and
assembly, not the most advanced ones.

12
00:00:36,712 --> 00:00:39,002
Can the world afford to
depend on one island?

13
00:00:39,123 --> 00:00:39,753
Comment.

